{"tool_name":"mole","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"mole","home":"http://mole.chemi.muni.cz","license":"Other","summary":"Location and basic characterization of channels in molecular structures.","addition_date":"2015-12-02T14:25:38Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:20:37.845956Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application","Web application"],"version":["2.0"],"collections":["CEITEC","Czech Republic","ELIXIR-CZ","LCC NCBR","MOLE"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:mole","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"david.sehnal@gmail.com","name":"David Sehnal","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Maintainer"]},{"email":"david.sehnal@gmail.com","name":"David Sehnal","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"jaroslav.koca@ceitec.muni.cz","name":"Jaroslav Ko\u010da","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"karel.berka@upol.cz","name":"Karel Berka","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"michal.otyepka@upol.cz","name":"Michal Otyepka","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"nancyblueberry@gmail.com","name":"Veronika Navr\u00e1tilov\u00e1","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"radka.svobodova@ceitec.muni.cz","name":"Radka Svobodov\u00e1 Va\u0159ekov\u00e1","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"email":"xpravda@ncbr.muni.cz","name":"Luk\u00e1\u0161 Pravda","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Maintainer"]},{"email":"xpravda@ncbr.muni.cz","name":"Luk\u00e1\u0161 Pravda","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"CEITEC","typeEntity":"Consortium"},{"name":"ELIXIR-CZ","typeEntity":"Consortium"},{"name":"Martin Petrek","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Masaryk University, Brno, Czech Republic","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Palack\u00fd University, Olomouc, Czech Republic","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["Citation instructions"],"url":"https://secure.jbs.elsevierhealth.com/action/showCitFormats?pii=S0969-2126%2807%2900375-9&doi=10.1016%2Fj.str.2007.10.007&code=cell-site"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://lcc.ncbr.muni.cz/whitezone/development/mole/web/documentation.php"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"PDB ID","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1127"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"},{"term":"mmCIF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1477"}]}],"note":"Identification of channels, tunnels, voids and pores together with their physicochemical properties calculation.","operation":[{"term":"Prediction and recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"},{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"},{"term":"Structure visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0570"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structural motif","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2878"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"},{"term":"XML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2332"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"MOLE","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-CZ","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1758-2946-5-39","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Channels and pores in biomacromolecules (proteins, nucleic acids and their complexes) play significant biological roles, e.g., in molecular recognition and enzyme substrate specificity. Results: We present an advanced software tool entitled MOLE 2.0, which has been designed to analyze molecular channels and pores. Benchmark tests against other available software tools showed that MOLE 2.0 is by comparison quicker, more robust and more versatile. As a new feature, MOLE 2.0 estimates physicochemical properties of the identified channels, i.e., hydropathy, hydrophobicity, polarity, charge, and mutability. We also assessed the variability in physicochemical properties of eighty X-ray structures of two members of the cytochrome P450 superfamily. Conclusion: Estimated physicochemical properties of the identified channels in the selected biomacromolecules corresponded well with the known functions of the respective channels. Thus, the predicted physicochemical properties may provide useful information about the potential functions of identified channels. The MOLE 2.0 software is available at http://mole.chemi.muni.cz. \u00a9 2013 Sehnal et al.; licensee Chemistry Central Ltd.","authors":[{"name":"Banas P."},{"name":"Berka K."},{"name":"Ionescu C.-M."},{"name":"Koca J."},{"name":"Navratilova V."},{"name":"Otyepka M."},{"name":"Pravda L."},{"name":"Sehnal D."},{"name":"Varekova R.S."}],"citationCount":256,"date":"2013-08-16T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Cheminformatics","title":"MOLE 2.0: Advanced approach for analysis of biomacromolecular channels"},"pmcid":"PMC3765717","pmid":"23953065","type":["Primary"]},{"doi":"10.1016/j.str.2007.10.007","metadata":{"abstract":"We have developed an algorithm, \"MOLE,\" for the rapid, fully automated location and characterization of molecular channels, tunnels, and pores. This algorithm has been made freely available on the Internet (http://mole.chemi.muni.cz/) and overcomes many of the shortcomings and limitations of the recently developed CAVER software. The core of our MOLE algorithm is a Dijkstra's path search algorithm, which is applied to a Voronoi mesh. Tests on a wide variety of biomolecular systems including gramicidine, acetylcholinesterase, cytochromes P450, potassium channels, DNA quadruplexes, ribozymes, and the large ribosomal subunit have demonstrated that the MOLE algorithm performs well. MOLE is thus a powerful tool for exploring large molecular channels, complex networks of channels, and molecular dynamics trajectories in which analysis of a large number of snapshots is required. \u00a9 2007 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Koca J."},{"name":"Kosinova P."},{"name":"Otyepka M."},{"name":"Petrek M."}],"citationCount":201,"date":"2007-11-13T00:00:00Z","journal":"Structure","title":"MOLE: A Voronoi Diagram-Based Explorer of Molecular Channels, Pores, and Tunnels"},"pmid":"17997961","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Enzymes","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0821"},{"term":"Membrane and lipoproteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0820"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Protein properties","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0123"},{"term":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"MOLE","home":"https://bio.tools/mole","license":"Other","version":"2.0","summary":"Location and basic characterization of channels in molecular structures.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:mole:2.0/app/mole.chemi.muni.cz","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{},"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"citation":true,"general":true},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":157,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":4,"year":"2014"},{"count":5,"year":"2026"},{"count":7,"year":"2017"},{"count":9,"year":"2019"},{"count":10,"year":"2025"},{"count":12,"year":"2015"},{"count":12,"year":"2016"},{"count":12,"year":"2018"},{"count":15,"y